# PixCull artifacts
models/*.onnx
models/*.pt
models/*.bin
models/*.safetensors
output/
v0_output/
*.xmp.bak
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
thumbs/

# v2.5 — the committed hermetic visual-smoke fixture run lives under an
# output/ dir (serve_demo._reload_run_from_disk requires that layout), so
# un-ignore just it (the broad output/ rule above would otherwise hide it).
# v3.51 — widened from `smoke_run` to any fixture run. The bare
# `output/` above matches a directory of that name at any depth, and the
# single-fixture exception meant the NEXT fixture was swallowed silently:
# v3.47's present_run existed locally, every test passed, and CI failed
# on a file that had never been in the commit. A per-name exception to a
# glob is a trap with a delay on it.
!tests/fixtures/*/output/
!tests/fixtures/*/output/**

# v3.63 — and samples/output, for the same reason and found the same
# way. The in-product "示例数据" button copies samples/output into a run
# and serves it; the bare `output/` above meant that directory could
# never be committed, so the button returned
# `500 samples/ not bundled with this build` for every user who ever
# clicked it. Second time this rule has eaten something load-bearing.
!samples/output/
!samples/output/**

# Internal / not for public repo
MARKET_ANALYSIS_*.md
.claude/
*.local
*.notes.md

# Per-developer or runtime config — these should stay private even on a
# fork. The taxonomy and config defaults live in code; anything written
# at runtime (DeepSeek key, license token, sync paths) belongs in the
# user's app-data dir, not the repo.
.envrc
.env
.env.local
*.token

# Lr plugin packaged bundles
lr_plugin/*.zip
lr_plugin/*.lrtemplate

# Large generated artifacts
*.h5
*.npz
face_library*.npz
*.bak

# P-PRO-4.2 — wedding-moment eval output (contains real photographer
# filenames; goldenset CSV is a local artifact, not a public dataset)
out_wedding_eval/
predictions*.csv

# Swift Package Manager build cache (generated by `swift build` /
# Xcode); large + machine-specific.  Don't commit.
mobile/PixCullCompanion/.build/
out_wedding_eval/realdemo01_smoke/
goldenset/v0.11/_eval_output/
goldenset/v0.11/training.csv

# modelscope upload cache (transient)
docs/screenshots/.ms_upload_cache

# v2.14 — local labeling sheets (may contain real photo filenames; keep private)
label_sheet*.csv

# v2.19 — local wheel build output
dist_wheel/

# v2.32 — cross-run library index: records REAL absolute photo paths,
# private to the machine. Never commit; it lives in ~/.pixcull/library/
# but guard against a stray local copy too.
library/
vectors.npy
manifest.jsonl

# v2.53 — the eval report names real photographs and describes what is in
# them ("越南渔妇", "戴斗笠牧鹅女"). Filenames plus content descriptions of
# a photographer's clients are exactly what the hygiene rules exist for,
# and a pre-push diff audit would only catch it the first time. The
# headline numbers are safe and live in the README; the per-row detail
# stays on the machine that produced it.
# Any eval report, not just the default filename: `m3 eval --out`
# takes a path, and the first run that used a suffix
# (docs/M3-EVAL-canon200.md) sailed straight past an exact match.
docs/M3-EVAL*.md
*-review.html
*-review.json
